{
  "film": "view-patch",
  "title": "PATCH: inside the sound",
  "description": "The deep dive into PATCH: read a patch's circuit, hear it properly, change it while you play, extend it from the node bank, protect what you love with locks, and keep your edit.",
  "fps": 30,
  "voice": {
    "voice": "af_heart",
    "speed": 0.9
  },
  "music": {
    "bed": "study",
    "bpm": 84,
    "meter": 4
  },
  "snap": "bar",
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "cold",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 11.2,
      "tail": 0.209,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "title",
      "music": "loop_a",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 1.2,
      "tail": 0.981,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "title1",
          "text": "PATCH is the inside of the sound.",
          "post": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "title2",
          "text": "One patch, in full, and playable while you take it apart.",
          "post": 0.6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-read",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 2.75,
      "tail": 0.087,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "read",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 1.0,
      "tail": 3.131,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "read1",
          "text": "This is a whole patch: real modules, joined by cables.",
          "post": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "read2",
          "text": "Sound flows left to right along the green ones.",
          "post": 0.4
        },
        {
          "id": "read3",
          "text": "A stack of saws makes the tone, a filter softens it, and a chorus widens it.",
          "post": 0.4
        },
        {
          "id": "read4",
          "text": "The last plate is always the envelope and the output.",
          "post": 0.6
        },
        {
          "id": "read5",
          "text": "Amber cables carry movement. This one is a slow LFO, sweeping the filter.",
          "post": 0.6
        },
        {
          "id": "read6",
          "text": "Every knob sits where it really is, in hertz, milliseconds and decibels.",
          "post": 0.8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-hear",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 2.75,
      "tail": 0.087,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "hear",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 0.6,
      "tail": 0.546,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "hear1",
          "text": "The play button plays the standard sample: five seconds, the same for every patch.",
          "post": 5.5
        },
        {
          "id": "hear2",
          "text": "That makes patches fair to compare. To judge a sound, play it.",
          "post": 4.0
        },
        {
          "id": "hear3",
          "text": "Above the rack, the model guesses how likely you are to prefer this patch, and says why.",
          "post": 0.6
        },
        {
          "id": "hear4",
          "text": "Point at a module, and the strip below says what it does, and what the model can't hear.",
          "post": 0.4
        },
        {
          "id": "hear5",
          "text": "The width of a chorus, for one, is invisible to it.",
          "post": 0.8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-change",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 2.75,
      "tail": 0.087,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "change",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 0.8,
      "tail": 0.435,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "change1",
          "text": "Turn any knob while you play, and the sound follows your hand.",
          "post": 2.5
        },
        {
          "id": "change2",
          "text": "Bypass a module, and it steps out of the sound.",
          "post": 2.5
        },
        {
          "id": "change3",
          "text": "Pull a cable, and the socket goes quiet. What it carried waits below, in HELD.",
          "post": 1.5
        },
        {
          "id": "change4",
          "text": "Command-Z puts it back.",
          "post": 2.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-add",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 2.75,
      "tail": 0.087,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "add",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 0.6,
      "tail": 0.436,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "add1",
          "text": "The node bank holds forty-two modules, ordered the way sound flows through them.",
          "post": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "add2",
          "text": "Click one, and it's in your hand. Every socket it fits lights up, and says what it would do.",
          "post": 0.6
        },
        {
          "id": "add3",
          "text": "Rest on a socket and press play, to hear it before anything changes.",
          "post": 2.5
        },
        {
          "id": "add4",
          "text": "Click the socket, and it's in.",
          "post": 3.0
        },
        {
          "id": "add5",
          "text": "A new sound source lights amber instead, because it would replace what's there.",
          "post": 0.8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-move",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 2.75,
      "tail": 0.088,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "move",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 0.6,
      "tail": 1.915,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "move1",
          "text": "Movement can come from a chain.",
          "post": 0.4
        },
        {
          "id": "move2",
          "text": "A sample and hold picks random values, a quantizer snaps them to A minor, and a slew glides between them.",
          "post": 0.4
        },
        {
          "id": "move3",
          "text": "Hold one key, and you get a melody.",
          "post": 3.0
        },
        {
          "id": "move4",
          "text": "Drop a shaper on a busy slot, and it wraps what's there instead of replacing it.",
          "post": 1.0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-steps",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 2.75,
      "tail": 0.087,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "steps",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 0.6,
      "tail": 2.835,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "steps1",
          "text": "Steps is a sequencer for timbre. Here it plays the filter.",
          "post": 0.4
        },
        {
          "id": "steps2",
          "text": "Draw its bars, up to eight, and the tone follows the pattern.",
          "post": 3.0
        },
        {
          "id": "steps3",
          "text": "Sync locks it to the tempo, here 84.",
          "post": 3.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-lock",
      "music": "loop_b",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 2.75,
      "tail": 0.087,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "lock",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 0.6,
      "tail": 1.12,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "lock1",
          "text": "Love part of a sound? Lock it: a knob by its dot, or a whole module by its square.",
          "post": 0.6
        },
        {
          "id": "lock2",
          "text": "Then press Evolve from this.",
          "post": 0.6
        },
        {
          "id": "lock3",
          "text": "Only what you left unlocked can change, and the new patch lands on the bench.",
          "post": 3.0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-keep",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 2.75,
      "tail": 0.087,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "keep",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 0.6,
      "tail": 2.03,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "keep1",
          "text": "Your changes join the bank only when you commit.",
          "post": 0.4
        },
        {
          "id": "keep2",
          "text": "Commit plays the original and your edit, in random order, and asks which is better.",
          "post": 5.0
        },
        {
          "id": "keep3",
          "text": "Either answer teaches the model.",
          "post": 0.6
        },
        {
          "id": "keep4",
          "text": "Already sure? Tick my edit is better, and it's filed as a claim.",
          "post": 0.8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-take",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 2.75,
      "tail": 0.087,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "take",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 0.6,
      "tail": 1.007,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "take1",
          "text": "Export a patch as a file, or as a picture of the rack.",
          "post": 0.6
        },
        {
          "id": "take2",
          "text": "The picture carries the patch inside. Drop either onto Auracle, and it opens, ready to play.",
          "post": 2.5
        },
        {
          "id": "take3",
          "text": "And EVOLVE's lineage keeps the history: each edit, each evolution, and what changed.",
          "post": 0.8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-together",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 2.75,
      "tail": 0.087,
      "lines": []
    },
    {
      "id": "together",
      "bed_db": -60,
      "lead": 1.5,
      "tail": 1.403,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "together1",
          "text": "All of it at once, at 84.",
          "post": 2.5
        },
        {
          "id": "together2",
          "text": "Shape the filter as it plays.",
          "post": 3.0
        },
        {
          "id": "together3",
          "text": "Add some grit after it.",
          "post": 4.0
        },
        {
          "id": "together4",
          "text": "Lock the filter, and commit it as yours.",
          "post": 3.0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "outro",
      "bed_db": 0,
      "lead": 0.8,
      "tail": 2.5,
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "outro1",
          "text": "Read it, change it, grow it, protect it, and keep what's yours.",
          "post": 0.7
        },
        {
          "id": "outro2",
          "text": "Next, EVOLVE: breeding sounds you like.",
          "post": 0.5
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}